abstract: >-
  Continuing the vision of software design sketched in Petricek's earlier
  essay, these fictional minutes recount the visit of a committee of software
  engineers and designers to Atelier, a workshop in another dimension where
  software is not written: it is curated. On the other side of the portal,
  software is understood as a shared medium for thinking: behavior is the
  design material, domain theories are made visible and discussable, AI acts
  as a colleague that expands judgment rather than replacing it, and
  governance is a legible property of the medium itself. The essay uses this
  design fiction to ask not what tool we need, but what medium we need to
  think together.
